{
  "_comment": "Canonical registry of every HTTP route exposed by packages/server's IPC server (consumed by the brainstorm desktop app and external clients). The contract-check gate at scripts/contract-checks/api-route-registry.mjs walks packages/server/src/server.ts and asserts every (method, path) pair matches this registry. This is NOT the platform-contract surface — that's a separate Zod-driven schema in packages/godmode/src/contract/schemas.ts. The brainstorm IPC server is its own thing; we lock it down for the same reason the CLI verb list is locked: nobody should be able to add a route without a deliberate registry edit. Parameterised paths use :id form regardless of the variable name in source.",
  "_categories": {
    "health": "Liveness check.",
    "discovery": "Lists products/tools/skills/models — read-only metadata surfaces.",
    "execution": "Triggers a tool, ChangeSet, dispatch, etc.",
    "chat": "Conversation surface — REST + SSE streaming.",
    "memory": "Persistent memory CRUD.",
    "audit": "Audit log + ChangeSet history.",
    "security": "Red-team / hardening surfaces.",
    "platform": "Inbound platform-event receiver (the brainstorm CLI side of the platform contract — it consumes events from products)."
  },
